---
// promptanddone.com/graphify: the GRAPHIFY pack (DM deliverable for the "graphify-codebase-map" reel). Prepared, not deployed.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const install = String.raw`uv tool install graphifyy      # note the double y (official package); or: pipx install graphifyy
graphify install               # registers the skill with Claude Code (other assistants: graphify install --platform <name>, graphify cursor install)`;
const run = String.raw`cd your-repo
graphify update .              # code only: tree-sitter, no LLM, no API key, nothing leaves your machine
open graphify-out/graph.html   # the clickable map; GRAPH_REPORT.md lists the "god nodes"`;
const ask = String.raw`graphify path "ModelAdmin" "HttpResponse"
Shortest path (2 hops):
  ModelAdmin --uses [INFERRED]--> SimpleTemplateResponse --inherits [EXTRACTED]--> HttpResponse

graphify explain "HttpResponse"      # one concept and its neighbours
graphify query "how does a request reach a view?"   # a scoped subgraph for a plain-language question`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Graphify: map any codebase for free, no AI tokens: Prompt &amp; Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · GRAPHIFY pack</p>
      <h1>Map a 3,000-file codebase in 43 seconds, with zero AI tokens.</h1>
      <p class="tag">Graphify (Apache-2.0, <a href="https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify">Graphify-Labs/graphify</a>) parses your code with tree-sitter and turns every class, call and import into one graph you can query. Every edge is tagged EXTRACTED (read from the code) or INFERRED (resolved by Graphify).</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">1</span> Install</h2><pre><code>{install}</code></pre>
      <p class="note">Needs Python 3.10+ and uv or pipx. The PyPI name is <code>graphifyy</code> (two y); other graphify packages are not official.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">2</span> Build the map</h2><pre><code>{run}</code></pre>
      <p>Or type <code>/graphify .</code> in Claude Code (Codex: <code>$graphify .</code>). Run <code>graphify claude install</code> in a project and Claude Code checks the graph before it greps (CLAUDE.md rule + a PreToolUse hook).</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">3</span> Ask how two things connect</h2><pre><code>{ask}</code></pre></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">4</span> What we measured (24 Oct 2026, M4 Pro, graphifyy 0.9.95)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Django</strong> (3,140 files in the corpus): 55,135 nodes, 131,306 edges, 2,095 communities in 42.6 to 42.9 s; report line "Token cost: 0 input, 0 output". 91% of edges EXTRACTED, 9% INFERRED.</li>
        <li><strong>Flask</strong> (106 files): 2,342 nodes, 3,749 edges in 2.2 s.</li>
        <li><strong>Query</strong>: <code>graphify path "ModelAdmin" "HttpResponse"</code> on Django took 1.79 to 1.81 s (mostly loading the 59 MB graph.json).</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Fair to say: this is the free, local, code-only part (tree-sitter). Docs, PDFs, images and video need a model backend. The paid Graphify Cloud is a separate product. We tested Claude Code with and without the graph on Flask and Django (Haiku, 8 runs): no consistent saving in tokens or cost, so we do not claim one. We tested the Claude Code install; Cursor and the other assistants are per the README.</p></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
